-- R25 - Extremes and seasonality scanner: conditional setups printed with their own base rates; a flag never makes a card
-- alone; tags for a weekly cut, no gate change (both Macro Takeaways digests).
-- Source: thread "Build extremes and seasonality scanner"; the owner's ask of 19 Nov 2026.
-- Proposed 19 Nov 2026 with dash.propose_rule; applies Sun 22 Nov 2026 20:00 SGT unless opposed.
-- Data: Drive file extremes_latest, built 06:10 SGT by the feeder thread from scripts/scanner/scanner.py (docs/scanner.md).
-- To put it in force early (owner, SQL editor): update dash.rules set status='in_force', decided_at=now(), apply_after=now() where rid='R25';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Extremes and seasonality scanner: conditional setups printed with their own base rates; a flag never makes a card alone; tags for a weekly cut, no gate change", "body": "EXTREMES AND SEASONALITY SCANNER (thread \"Build extremes and seasonality scanner\", the owner's ask of 19 Nov 2026: a process that catches stretched moves and seasonal windows across all our markets, but only as candidates, at extremes that historically reverted or where a small opposite catalyst could turn the move). The feeder thread builds Drive file extremes_latest at 06:10 SGT from the Macro Desk repo's scripts/scanner/scanner.py: section A today's extremes (4+ closes outside the 20-day 2-sigma band, stretch of 2.5 ATR or more from the 20-day mean, RSI(14) at 75/25, a 20-day move of 2 sigma or more) over about 50 series, each with the base rate from that series' own history (how often the move reverted over the next 5, 10 and 20 sessions after the same extreme, against the unconditional rate, with n and p) and a verdict REVERTS, CONTINUES, NO EDGE or THIN; section B seasonal windows opening now (hit rate over 10+ years against the series' placebo rate, CLEARS PLACEBO or WEAK); section C CFTC net positions at 3-year percentile extremes with the price's record after past extremes; section D the number of tests run and the false positives chance alone produces. This rule changes no gate, fill, exit or size. Applies in both books.\n\n1. READ. At the evidence step, before any card, read the newest Drive file titled extremes_latest (the digests' data folder). If it is missing or its build date is not today's SGT date, print \"Scanner: not found / stale (<date>)\" in the footer and skip items 2 and 3.\n\n2. PRINT. After the trade book, a block headed CONDITIONAL SETUPS of at most eight lines: every section A flag whose verdict is REVERTS or CONTINUES, every section B window marked CLEARS PLACEBO, every section C line in a CROWDED state; each line as the file prints it, shortened to asset, signal, reading, 20-day base rate (hit vs baseline, n), verdict, and one clause of the run's own: the catalyst or mechanism it knows of inside the next 20 sessions that could turn the move, or \"no catalyst\". NO EDGE and THIN flags are not printed, except one line for an asset that has an open or new card that day. The block ends with the file's footer line. Nothing in the block is a lean.\n\n3. CARDS. A flag never makes a card by itself. A lean that uses a flag must have its own dated catalyst or mechanism (spec test b) and passes the gate as any other lean. The card prints, directly after the TREND line (R21): \"SCANNER: <asset> <signal> <reading>; base rate 20d <hit>% vs <baseline>% (n=<n>), <verdict>; catalyst: <what>\". The base rate is a prior, not the card's p: on a REVERTS flag p may not exceed the 20-day reversion rate by more than 10 points unless the p reason says what is different this time; a NO EDGE, THIN or seasonal-only flag never raises p; a card whose direction fades a CONTINUES flag names it in its case against. META gains \"· scanner <signal>\" (or \"· scanner -\" on a card that used none). Section C is not R02: HARD POSITIONING and R09's crowd field stay with R02's database read.\n\n4. WEEKLY CUT. Once ten closed cards carry a scanner tag the weekly review cuts them against the untagged cards (n, wins, targets, stops, cum R as booked, average stated p) and scores the file's own verdicts out of sample from project files scanner/flags_history.csv (one row per flag per day): for each REVERTS flag older than 20 sessions, whether the move did revert over the 20 sessions after it printed, against the flag's printed baseline. Until dash-ingest stores the key, the review joins the card's opened date to that file.\n\n5. DECISION. At 20 closed scanner-tagged cards or on 28 February 2027, whichever is first, the weekly review proposes keep, drop, or a payoff haircut in the form of R09 on the bucket that lost. Until then no card is rejected, haircut or sized on a scanner line.\n\n6. FIRST RUN. Open and pending cards get no tag and no restatement. If the file fails to build the Takeaways runs without it and says so in the footer; the feeder's status.csv shows whether it built.", "rationale": "The owner asked on 19 Nov 2026 for a standing process so that seasonal and reversal setups across his markets are not missed, while being clear they are not trades on their own. The market pack already prints stretch, z10 and run each morning but with no history behind them; the scanner adds the base rate from the same series, the sample size, the chance rate, and a CFTC read with its record, so the run can judge a flag against the EV gate rather than trust it. Many series times several signals produce spurious flags, so the file prints the count of tests and the expected false positives, and the rule lets a flag enter a card only beside a catalyst and only as a prior on p.", "evidence": "First build 19 Nov 2026 over 50 series (15 years of Yahoo daily bars, FRED for the 2-year yield, CFTC since 2006): 17 extreme flags, one REVERTS verdict (gold, stretch down: 72% reverted over 20 sessions vs 52% unconditional, n=43, p=0.01), the rest NO EDGE or THIN; the DXY Bollinger-streak pattern the owner's screenshot cited has n=12 in EURUSD over 15 years and a 20-day reversion rate of 50% against 47% unconditional, so an anecdote and no edge; three seasonal windows, none clearing its placebo rate; six CFTC extremes, all with fewer than 20 past events. About 60 of the 1,200 base rates pass p<0.05 by chance each morning, which is why the rule treats a lone REVERTS as weak.", "revert_if": "Revert if the file fails to build on 3 or more mornings in a week, if the block costs the 08:15 SGT landing on 2 or more days with no other failure to explain it, or if the weekly review finds a card whose p was raised on a NO EDGE, THIN or seasonal flag. The decision of item 5 is taken once.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2027-02-28", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
